cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Power losses and effective conductivity of a nanocrystalline ribbon
  toroidal core with symmetrical air gaps: data and analysis code
message: >-
  If you use these data or this code, please cite the archived release
  listed under identifiers.
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  Core losses of one FINEMET-type nanocrystalline ribbon toroidal core,
  measured from 50 Hz to 20 kHz at six temperatures between 20 and 120 C in
  three states: ungapped, with two symmetrical 0.17 mm air gaps, and with
  two symmetrical 0.47 mm air gaps. For each of the 126 operating points a
  three-dimensional finite-element model was tuned until it reproduced the
  measured loss; the tuned scalar is the effective conductivity of the
  homogenised core material. The repository holds the measured losses, the
  identified conductivities, the finite-element cases that produced them,
  and the analysis code that fits and compares four descriptions of their
  frequency dependence.
